OL,3,GNEWSALargest woodland bat survey a
OL,4,A'nice story of AI for good'
OL,5,
OL,6,FBritain's largest ever woodland survey
OL,7,Fof bats would "simply not have been
OL,8,Ffeasible" without AI, scientists say.
OL,10,FResearchers left devices on poles among
OL,11,Fthe trees of 310 woodlands across
OL,12,FBritain, recording 98 million bat calls
OL,13,Fover three years, which would have
OL,14,Ftaken more than 30 years to analyse
OL,15,Fwithout AI.
OL,17,FSome of Britain's rarest and most
OL,18,Fthreatened bats, including the
OL,19,Fred-listed Barbastelle, have been
OL,20,Frecorded in the south-west of England,
OL,21,Fincluding Somerset, Devon, Cornwall and
OL,22,FDorset.
OL,23,APub: 30-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,347,340,200,160,0,100
